.TH BALLISTICS 2
.SH NAME
ballistics \- reusable projectile-acceleration kernels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B include "danby/ballistics.m";
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ballistics
computes the instantaneous acceleration of a projectile subject to
quadratic drag, Magnus lift (or spin-induced curve), gravity, and an
optional constant vertical force.
.PP
.B acceleration
evaluates the planar (x, y) case, taking velocity components
.IR vx , vy ,
drag and lift coefficients, a spin rate, gravity, and an extra
.I verticalforce
term (used for a boost or downdraft); it returns the resulting
.IR ax , ay
acceleration pair.
.PP
.B acceleration3
evaluates the three-dimensional case, taking velocity components
.IR vx , vy , vz ,
a drag coefficient, a Magnus coefficient, a spin vector
.IR spinx , spiny , spinz ,
and gravity; it returns the
.IR ax , ay , az
acceleration triple, with the Magnus term computed as the cross
product of spin and velocity.
.PP
Callers integrate these accelerations themselves (typically with
.IR numerics 's
RK4 stepper) to produce a trajectory; the module holds no state of
its own.
.SH SOURCE
.B /module/danby/ballistics.m
.br
.B /appl/danby/ballistics.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR flight3d (2),
.IR numerics (2)
